## 3. Validation checklist

**From the Bastion:**

| # | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `ssh target 'whoami; hostname'` | Key passphrase prompt (no account password), then `secadmin` / `target` |
| 2 | `ssh -o PubkeyAuthentication=no -o PreferredAuthentications=password secadmin@target` | `Permission denied (publickey)` |
| 3 | `ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_lab root@target` | `Permission denied (publickey)` |
| 4 | `ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_lab operator1@target` | `Permission denied (publickey)` |
| 5 | `grep target ~/.ssh/known_hosts` | Entry present (hashed) and `StrictHostKeyChecking yes` set |

**On the Target:**

| # | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|
| 6 | `sudo sshd -t` | No output |
| 7 | `sudo sshd -T \| grep -E '^(permitrootlogin\|passwordauthentication\|authenticationmethods\|allowgroups\|maxauthtries\|allowtcpforwarding\|loglevel)'` | `no`, `no`, `publickey`, `lab-admins lab-operators`, `3`, `no`, `VERBOSE` |
| 8 | `ls -l /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/` | `00-hardening.conf` present, `root root`, `644` |
| 9 | `stat -c '%a %U %n' ~/.ssh ~/.ssh/authorized_keys` (as `secadmin`) | `700 secadmin`, `600 secadmin` |
| 10 | `systemctl is-active ssh.socket ssh.service` | Informational. Record which is `active`. |
| 11 | `sudo ss -tlnp \| grep sshd` | Listening on port 22 only |
| 12 | `sudo journalctl -u ssh --no-pager \| grep Accepted \| tail -2` | Shows `Accepted publickey for secadmin ... ED25519 SHA256:...` (the VERBOSE fingerprint) |
| 13 | `sudo systemctl is-active fail2ban` and `sudo fail2ban-client status` | `active`; jail list contains `sshd` |
| 14 | Ban test from Step E | Bastion IP banned, then unbanned, then login works again |
| 15 | After closing NAT: `ip route` | No default route |

Save outputs as `~/evidence/p04.txt` on the Bastion if you want them for the README, and never include private keys or passphrases. Your host-key fingerprint comparison from Step A is nice README material too.
